      "proof_trace": "The Supabase query at L15-20 chains only `.is('deleted_at', null)` and two `.order()` calls — no `.limit()` or `.range()` is applied, and `req.query` is never inspected for pagination params. There is no PAGE_LIMIT enforcement anywhere in the handler or in the auth middleware. The sole access control is a static Bearer token (`API_AUTH_TOKEN`), which is a single point of failure but not a substitute for pagination.",
      "attack_scenario": "An attacker who obtains the static Bearer token (e.g., via SSRF against the stem-system server reading `STEM_BOT_API_BEARER_TOKEN`, git history exposure, or server misconfiguration) can issue a single `GET /api/members` request to dump the entire active-member database — discord UIDs, student numbers, generation, and status — in one unbounded response.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-api-request-inv-008"
    },
    "text": "Bulk member enumeration endpoint must enforce pagination to prevent full database dump.",
    "assertion": "forall GET /api/members: response.members.length <= PAGE_LIMIT",
    "covers": "SG-005",
    "severity": "MEDIUM",
    "type": "invariant"
  }
}

